From: =?UTF-8?q?Miguel=20=C3=81ngel=20Pastor=20Olivar?=
 <migue@planetscale.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:30:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] mysqlctl: stop waiting for a closed connection's
 replacement when the context ends
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Recycling a closed pooled connection opens its replacement before Recycle
returns, under the pool's lifetime context rather than the caller's. A
timed-out query closes its connection, so on a mysqld that accepts the
socket but does not answer, the caller stayed blocked on the replacement
handshake long after its deadline, holding the shard lock with it.

Wait for the replacement only until the caller's context ends, and let it
finish in the background after that.

Signed-off-by: Miguel Ángel Pastor Olivar <migue@planetscale.com>
---
